WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.950
Which cloud?

2
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.775
A GCC Moderate estate's subscriptions
are commercial Azure, so the settings

3
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:10.600
name the Azure Cloud, and the source
links are on management dot azure dot com.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.587
There's no default: an
unknown cloud name throws.

5
00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:19.328
As a side note for GCC High and DoD estates,
Azure Government uses its own cloud

6
00:00:19.328 --> 00:00:25.338
setting and its own Resource Manager host,
management dot us gov cloud api dot net.

7
00:00:25.338 --> 00:00:30.153
Every Service Health sample on Learn links
the Azure Government portal as well as

8
00:00:30.153 --> 00:00:33.412
the global one, but an explicit
availability statement

9
00:00:33.412 --> 00:00:36.599
for the table in Azure
Government is not yet specified.

10
00:00:36.599 --> 00:00:39.138
The danger is a reader in the wrong cloud.

11
00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:43.639
Azure Government subscriptions read from
the commercial cloud return nothing,

12
00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:45.788
and the gate would pass on an empty list.

13
00:00:45.788 --> 00:00:50.450
So the live invoker refuses an Azure
command line set to another cloud.
